```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class FactorialCalculator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
        try {
            int number = Integer.parseInt(scanner.nextLine());
            if (number < 0) {
                System.out.println("Please enter a non-negative number.");
            } else {
                System.out.println("Factorial of " + number + " is: " + calculateFactorial(number));
            }
        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
            System.out.println("Invalid input! Please enter a valid integer.");
        }
    }

    private static long calculateFactorial(int number) {
        if (number == 0) {
            return 1;
        }
        long factorial = 1;
        for (int i = 1; i <= number; i++) {
            factorial *= i;
        }
        return factorial;
    }
}
```

This code reads an input from the user, checks if it's a valid non-negative integer, and calculates the factorial using a simple loop. It handles `NumberFormatException` to manage cases where the input is not a valid integer.

